WEBVTT

00:01.800 --> 00:05.150
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.250 --> 00:08.734
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.769 --> 00:12.420
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:12.438 --> 00:15.423
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:15.458 --> 00:18.926
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.960 --> 00:22.246
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:22.280 --> 00:23.814
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.865 --> 00:25.481
♪ Laugh and cry

00:25.532 --> 00:27.532
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.706 --> 00:36.574
All right, I'm going
to the store.

00:36.608 --> 00:37.741
Anybody need anything?

00:37.775 --> 00:40.644
Yeah, can you get me a chess set
and a backwards hat?

00:40.678 --> 00:42.378
I got some inner-city
school kids

00:42.412 --> 00:43.779
I gotta inspire tomorrow.

00:43.813 --> 00:46.297
Okay, Darius,
point to the king.

00:49.485 --> 00:52.653
That's right.
It's you.

00:52.687 --> 00:54.203
Hey, Lois. Doesn't, uh,
somebody have

00:54.237 --> 00:55.721
a birthday coming up
this week?

00:55.756 --> 00:57.940
Oh, it's nice of you
to remember, Brian,

00:57.975 --> 01:00.342
but, frankly, I'd rather
let this one slip by.

01:00.376 --> 01:02.761
I don't need to be reminded
how old I'm gettin'.

01:02.795 --> 01:04.079
You know, it's funny.

01:04.113 --> 01:06.047
You keep so busy
with your kids,

01:06.082 --> 01:07.681
time just seems
to slip away,

01:07.716 --> 01:09.900
and then you turn
around one day and...

01:09.935 --> 01:11.701
Okay, bye.
Stop making noise.

01:11.735 --> 01:13.603
(sighs)

01:15.004 --> 01:16.822
You know, Peter, I know
Lois is downplaying it,

01:16.856 --> 01:18.607
but I think she might
actually appreciate it

01:18.641 --> 01:20.007
if we threw her
a party.

01:20.042 --> 01:21.776
Maybe even
a surprise party.

01:21.810 --> 01:23.227
That's a great
idea, Brian!

01:23.261 --> 01:24.477
Yeah, I love parties.

01:24.512 --> 01:26.880
I mean, I had a great time
at my baby shower.

01:26.914 --> 01:28.530
Well, after opening all
these gifts,

01:28.565 --> 01:30.666
I could use a little wine
right now myself.

01:30.700 --> 01:32.283
(chuckles) Glug,
glug, glug, glug.

01:32.318 --> 01:34.769
Can you imagine?!
(laughs)

01:34.803 --> 01:36.787
(sobbing)

01:36.821 --> 01:40.723
I'm sorry. My hormones are
just crazy right now!

01:45.395 --> 01:48.014
(both laughing)

01:50.266 --> 01:52.700
Stewie, you want
a Mommy rocket ride?

01:52.734 --> 01:53.901
What?
What do you mean?

01:53.935 --> 01:55.703
Here we go!
Get ready for blastoff!

01:55.737 --> 01:56.687
(bone cracks)

01:56.721 --> 01:58.187
Ow! Son of a bitch!

01:58.222 --> 01:59.155
(gasps)

01:59.189 --> 02:01.189
Oh, my God, Stewie,
are you all right?

02:01.224 --> 02:03.792
Nice throw,
Casey Anthony.

02:04.944 --> 02:07.862
Oh, my God, I hope the guys
at Sears portrait studio

02:07.896 --> 02:09.763
will be able to retouch this.

02:09.797 --> 02:10.964
What am I saying?

02:10.998 --> 02:13.166
Of course they will.
They're Sears.

02:13.200 --> 02:14.733
What the deuce?

02:14.768 --> 02:15.968
Well, hello there.

02:16.002 --> 02:17.952
I say, you're
a cute little fellow.

02:17.987 --> 02:21.072
Tell me something: What do you
think about Rose McGowan?

02:21.123 --> 02:23.156
Yeah, she makes
my turtlehead go in, too.

02:23.191 --> 02:25.076
How about Michelle Rodriguez?

02:25.110 --> 02:26.877
Yeah, me too, kinda, right?

02:26.911 --> 02:28.795
You know, she's got
like a cute tomboy thing

02:28.830 --> 02:31.047
where you feel like you could
play softball with her,

02:31.081 --> 02:33.215
and then later on,
give her the old sau-seege.

02:33.250 --> 02:34.449
I like you.

02:34.483 --> 02:36.584
I can tell we're going
to be good friends.

02:36.619 --> 02:40.087
We've got that unspoken bond
that all bald guys have.

02:42.873 --> 02:44.207
I thought
he'd never leave.

02:44.241 --> 02:45.425
Me neither.

02:45.476 --> 02:46.843
(slurping)

02:49.178 --> 02:50.929
(both sigh)

02:50.963 --> 02:51.962
Yeah.

02:53.465 --> 02:55.515
Aw, did you guys
just do the thing?

02:59.053 --> 03:01.503
Okay, we'll see you soon.
Bye. All right, you guys,

03:01.538 --> 03:04.073
that was Lois. She's gonna be
here in ten minutes.

03:04.107 --> 03:06.675
Dad, how did you get Mom out of
the house so we could decorate?

03:06.710 --> 03:08.276
Well, Chris, I constructed

03:08.310 --> 03:11.045
a very elaborate
fake grocery store.

03:11.797 --> 03:12.829
Oh, my God!

03:12.864 --> 03:15.198
Are these pickles really
only 39 cents?!

03:15.233 --> 03:16.265
That's right, ma'am.

03:16.299 --> 03:18.901
Wow! This is incredible!

03:20.270 --> 03:22.404
(wind whistling)

03:22.438 --> 03:24.905
What the hell's
going on here?

03:28.426 --> 03:30.259
And over here are my toys.

03:30.294 --> 03:32.961
This is my fire truck,
my Slinky, my Silly Putty.

03:32.995 --> 03:34.596
You know, Silly Putty's
awesome,

03:34.630 --> 03:37.364
but you know what's
really cool? Serious Putty.

03:37.399 --> 03:40.317
Oh, this looks
like fun!

03:40.352 --> 03:42.786
It says I have cancer.

03:42.820 --> 03:44.522
We thought it would be better

03:44.556 --> 03:46.489
if you heard it
from chemicals in an egg.

03:46.524 --> 03:47.640
Hey, Stewie,
you better come down.

03:47.691 --> 03:48.641
The party's
about to start.

03:48.676 --> 03:50.576
What is that?
Is that a turtle?

03:50.610 --> 03:52.611
Yes, Brian.
I found him at the park.

03:52.645 --> 03:53.911
I named him Sheldon.

03:53.946 --> 03:56.080
Oh, and get this:
I brought him home today,

03:56.115 --> 03:58.048
and coincidentally
this is the day

03:58.082 --> 03:59.916
Rupert started
working out again.

03:59.951 --> 04:01.685
So transparent.

04:01.719 --> 04:03.452
Rupert?
What happened to your eye?

04:03.487 --> 04:05.604
Brian, did you pull
one of Rupert's eyes off?

04:05.639 --> 04:07.138
No. Why would I do that?

04:07.173 --> 04:08.373
Maybe your
turtle did it.

04:08.407 --> 04:10.008
Nonsense. Sheldon
is a gentle soul.

04:10.042 --> 04:11.308
He wouldn't hurt anybody.

04:11.342 --> 04:12.876
Well, come on.
Let's get downstairs.

04:12.911 --> 04:14.277
Lois will be here
any minute.

04:31.276 --> 04:33.143
ALL:
Surprise!

04:33.177 --> 04:35.145
Yay!
Birthday!

04:35.179 --> 04:36.912
Oh, my God!

04:36.946 --> 04:38.247
Happy birthday,
Lois!

04:38.281 --> 04:39.997
You guys shouldn't
have done this!

04:40.032 --> 04:43.000
Hey, anytime you can celebrate
the end of someone's periods.

04:43.035 --> 04:45.368
Everyone, everyone,
I have something to say.

04:45.403 --> 04:48.954
To my dearest Lois
on her birthday.

04:48.989 --> 04:51.056
What a journey
we've had together.

04:51.091 --> 04:54.058
You know, life has a way
of changing things.

04:54.093 --> 04:56.860
What were once two firm,
impressive mountain peaks

04:56.895 --> 04:59.797
have become a barren,
strip-mined, muddy landslide

04:59.831 --> 05:01.397
that droops ever downward.

05:01.431 --> 05:04.167
What were once pink
and succulent rose petals

05:04.201 --> 05:06.502
now take the form
of the shredded, raggedy,

05:06.537 --> 05:10.338
blown-out endpiece of a
practical joker's exploding cigar.

05:10.373 --> 05:11.473
Peter, that-
that's enough.

05:11.507 --> 05:13.108
Lois, you may not be

05:13.142 --> 05:14.942
the young filly you were
when I met you,

05:14.976 --> 05:17.444
but you're still my
reliable old plow horse

05:17.478 --> 05:18.745
who's there each day

05:18.779 --> 05:20.713
to pull the plow,
to help around the barn,

05:20.748 --> 05:23.949
and let the husband horse-slap
a batch at her now and then.

05:23.983 --> 05:26.150
Well, I guess that's it.

05:26.185 --> 05:27.418
I love you, sweetheart.

05:27.452 --> 05:30.253
And I have a lovely gift
of the batchslapping variety

05:30.288 --> 05:32.656
waiting for you when I'm just
the right amount of drunk.

05:32.690 --> 05:33.673
To Lois!

05:33.708 --> 05:34.874
ALL:
To Lois!

05:36.693 --> 05:38.977
(sobbing, door shuts)

05:39.011 --> 05:40.378
Lois!
Mom!

05:40.412 --> 05:41.913
Geez, what the hell's
her problem?

05:41.947 --> 05:43.847
Peter, she was already
feeling insecure about her age,

05:43.882 --> 05:46.184
and then you went and gave her
that horrible speech!

05:46.218 --> 05:47.251
I don't blame her.

05:47.285 --> 05:49.353
Nobody likes to be
humiliated in public.

05:49.387 --> 05:50.721
I'm King Stewie!

05:50.755 --> 05:52.505
I rule with
an iron fist!

05:52.539 --> 05:56.208
La, la-la, la-la la-la!
Look at me! Ooh!

05:56.242 --> 05:58.376
In my office. Now.

06:01.880 --> 06:03.347
Hey, any of you guys
seen your mother?

06:03.381 --> 06:04.797
She never came
to bed last night,

06:04.832 --> 06:06.065
and I can't find
her anywhere.

06:06.100 --> 06:07.233
(car horn beeps)

06:07.268 --> 06:09.184
What the hell?

06:09.219 --> 06:13.371
♪

06:17.642 --> 06:20.426
Hey, sluts!

06:20.460 --> 06:23.529
OMG, stop staring at me,
please-'kay-thanks.

06:23.563 --> 06:25.230
Mom, are you okay?

06:25.264 --> 06:26.765
Lois, what's goin' on?

06:26.800 --> 06:28.484
I'm what's
goin' on, Peter.

06:28.518 --> 06:30.652
I got highlights,
I went shopping,

06:30.686 --> 06:32.253
and I had my...

06:32.288 --> 06:35.255
So it's tighter now.

06:35.290 --> 06:38.541
Peter, I think Lois might be
having a midlife crisis.

06:38.575 --> 06:41.309
Come on, dudes!
Who wants to hop in my wheels

06:41.344 --> 06:44.112
and head to the beach
for some ultimate Frisbee?

06:45.131 --> 06:47.464
Yeah, Sheldon, I'm with you.

06:52.453 --> 06:54.720
I can't... I can't do that.

07:01.317 --> 07:02.594
Hey, tweeps!

07:02.595 --> 07:04.262
JK, I don't follow you,
you're lame.

07:04.297 --> 07:07.432
But look who just got
herself a sick new tat.

07:07.467 --> 07:09.468
MEG:
Oh, my God, Mom!

07:09.502 --> 07:11.519
I know,
I can't believe it either.

07:11.553 --> 07:14.422
I guess one of my flaws
is I'm just kinda brave.

07:14.456 --> 07:15.922
No, that's great actually,
because now

07:15.956 --> 07:19.158
anyone walking behind you
will know that you had $60.

07:19.192 --> 07:20.926
Wow! That is awesome, Lois!

07:20.960 --> 07:22.728
Your bum looks like
an NBA guy's arm.

07:22.762 --> 07:24.695
'Cept it's not payin'
someone to install

07:24.730 --> 07:26.431
a PlayStation in a car.

07:26.465 --> 07:28.131
Lois, you do know
that's permanent?

07:28.166 --> 07:29.366
Good. Then that means

07:29.400 --> 07:31.700
my ass is gonna
look young forever.

07:33.837 --> 07:38.957
Guys, I, uh, I gotta go
shoot one into the sink.

07:38.991 --> 07:40.124
What's going on?

07:40.158 --> 07:42.326
Mom's acting and dressing
like a 20-year-old.

07:42.360 --> 07:43.910
I know, and I'm
worried about her.

07:43.944 --> 07:46.028
You can't just pretend
to be something you're not.

07:46.063 --> 07:48.214
Yes, just ask
Edward Scissorhands.

07:48.248 --> 07:51.717
Okay, now, I'm an excellent
night nurse, so you two get

07:51.752 --> 07:54.820
some much-deserved sleep
and don't worry about a thing.

07:54.854 --> 07:58.255
I will take such loving care
of this wonderful little gift.

07:58.290 --> 07:59.957
And when you wake up,
well-rested,

07:59.991 --> 08:02.492
your precious little baby
will be smiling

08:02.526 --> 08:04.194
as bright as the sun.

08:05.929 --> 08:07.296
It's dead.

08:10.866 --> 08:13.099
And while I remind you
I can't read yet,

08:13.134 --> 08:15.068
I can only imagine
Madeline would say,

08:15.102 --> 08:17.636
"Take me out of this
disgusting French hospital

08:17.671 --> 08:19.205
and find me some
real parents."

08:19.239 --> 08:21.307
Ah! Paper cut!

08:21.341 --> 08:22.640
A razor blade?!

08:22.675 --> 08:26.260
Who the hell uses a razor blade
as a bookmark?!

08:28.214 --> 08:29.913
All right,
very funny, Stewie.

08:29.948 --> 08:31.331
What?
What do you mean, what?

08:31.366 --> 08:33.567
You replaced my Jack Daniels
with flat Diet Coke.

08:33.601 --> 08:34.851
No, I didn't.

08:34.885 --> 08:37.353
And you're noticing this
at 8:20 in the morning?

08:37.387 --> 08:38.620
What has happened
to your life?

08:38.654 --> 08:39.955
Do you need to talk?

08:39.989 --> 08:41.490
Just stay away
from my booze!

08:41.524 --> 08:42.623
It wasn't me, Brian.

08:42.657 --> 08:43.874
Well, if it wasn't you,
who was it?

08:43.909 --> 08:45.125
I mean, there's a lot
of weird stuff

08:45.160 --> 08:46.260
going on
around here lately.

08:46.294 --> 08:48.545
Just yesterday, somebody gave
Peter a "hotbutt."

08:48.579 --> 08:50.796
♪ La, la, la, la, la,
regular life ♪

08:50.830 --> 08:53.048
♪ La, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la, l... ♪

08:53.082 --> 08:54.216
(screams)

08:54.267 --> 08:56.184
And then somebody replaced
Meg's sleeping pills

08:56.218 --> 08:57.485
with Alka-Seltzer.

08:59.520 --> 09:01.555
People are gonna miss me
when I'm...

09:01.589 --> 09:04.190
(belching)

09:04.224 --> 09:06.208
Well, I'm sure there's a
perfectly logical explanation

09:06.243 --> 09:07.259
for those things.

09:07.294 --> 09:08.861
Sometimes you just...

09:08.895 --> 09:11.146
Whoa, that was close.

09:11.181 --> 09:13.548
Yeah, how'd
that thing fall over?

09:18.620 --> 09:20.970
Okay, who replaced
my glasses with forks?

09:21.004 --> 09:22.638
I mean, they're real good
for seeing forks

09:22.673 --> 09:24.306
but not much else.

09:27.376 --> 09:30.144
LOIS: Peter, can you come down
to the laundry room?

09:30.178 --> 09:31.278
Ugh, son of a bitch.

09:31.313 --> 09:32.812
If she washed
my belt again,

09:32.846 --> 09:35.682
I am gonna hit her
with my dry, withered belt.

09:35.716 --> 09:36.882
What is it, Lois?

09:36.916 --> 09:38.183
I was watching...

09:38.218 --> 09:41.919
Whoa, Lois, what the
hell are you doing?

09:41.954 --> 09:45.322
Do me, Peter, do me right here
in the basement.

09:45.356 --> 09:48.425
Y-You mean this room we're in
or your bum?

09:48.459 --> 09:51.595
No, this room, Peter,
right here on the carpet.

09:51.629 --> 09:52.829
Oh, so you mean the front.

09:52.863 --> 09:54.647
Just get over here
and kiss me.

09:54.681 --> 09:57.765
Let's have sex on all
the clean, folded laundry.

09:57.800 --> 10:00.552
Wow, Lois, I got to say,
I like this new you.

10:00.586 --> 10:01.719
I like it a lot.

10:01.754 --> 10:03.654
(both giggling)

10:03.688 --> 10:06.022
Oh, Peter!

10:06.056 --> 10:07.924
Oh, Peter, yes!
Yeah.

10:07.958 --> 10:09.592
Oh, I'm on fire.
Yeah.

10:09.626 --> 10:11.660
Take me, you filthy bastard.
Yeah, oh.

10:11.694 --> 10:13.161
Destroy me and this laundry.
Oh, yeah.

10:13.195 --> 10:15.529
Yeah, here, put Meg's
bra in your mouth.

10:15.564 --> 10:17.565
Oh, my God,
that's so disturbing.

10:17.599 --> 10:19.065
I know, gross.

10:19.099 --> 10:20.500
Yeah, and my hearing's
a lot better,

10:20.534 --> 10:23.235
so I hear, like,
suction and stuff.

10:23.269 --> 10:27.405
♪ "All I wanna do is have
a little fun before I die" ♪

10:27.439 --> 10:31.175
♪ Says the man next to me
out of nowhere ♪

10:32.177 --> 10:33.427
♪ The good people of the world

10:33.462 --> 10:36.162
♪ Are washing their cars
on their lunch break ♪

10:36.197 --> 10:38.231
♪ Hosing and scrubbing
as best they can ♪

10:38.266 --> 10:40.766
♪ In skirts and suits

10:40.800 --> 10:44.752
♪ They drive
their shiny Datsuns and Buicks ♪

10:44.787 --> 10:48.088
♪ Back to the phone company,
the record store, too ♪

10:48.106 --> 10:50.424
♪ Well, they're nothing
like Billy and me ♪

10:50.458 --> 10:54.777
♪ 'Cause all I wanna do
is have some fun ♪

10:54.811 --> 10:58.780
♪ I got a feeling
I'm not the only one ♪

10:58.814 --> 11:01.982
♪ All I wanna do
is have some fun ♪

11:02.017 --> 11:06.936
♪ I got a feeling
I'm not the only one ♪

11:06.954 --> 11:10.456
♪ All I want to do
is have some fun ♪

11:10.491 --> 11:17.111
♪ Until the sun comes up
over Santa Monica Boulevard. ♪

11:33.042 --> 11:34.007
(sniffs)

11:34.042 --> 11:35.008
(screams)

11:35.043 --> 11:36.376
Sheldon. What are you doing?

11:36.411 --> 11:38.344
Get back in your bowl
where you belong.

11:42.032 --> 11:46.134
Well, long as I'm up, I might
as well go spit in Lois's mouth.

11:48.870 --> 11:50.971
Sheldon?

11:55.693 --> 11:57.176
(gasps)

11:57.211 --> 11:58.695
(panting)

12:01.114 --> 12:02.397
Come on, Stewie.

12:02.432 --> 12:04.098
He's just a little turtle.

12:04.132 --> 12:06.133
He can't hurt you.

12:12.122 --> 12:13.188
(screams)

12:18.861 --> 12:20.811
(hissing)

12:20.845 --> 12:22.863
(toilet flushes)

12:25.332 --> 12:26.899
(sighs)

12:26.933 --> 12:29.167
Get out!

12:34.473 --> 12:36.490
(chirping)

12:44.098 --> 12:45.881
(squawking)

12:45.915 --> 12:47.416
(neck snaps)

12:53.121 --> 12:55.121
(dance music playing)

12:58.174 --> 12:59.624
Isn't this epic, Peter?

12:59.642 --> 13:01.809
That DJ has got
some mad skills.

13:01.844 --> 13:04.178
(sighs) You think they
sell Anacin at the bar?

13:04.229 --> 13:05.179
Come on.

13:05.230 --> 13:06.897
Get up and dance
with me, Peter.

13:06.931 --> 13:08.265
This place is sick.

13:08.299 --> 13:09.366
Hells yeah!

13:09.400 --> 13:11.835
It is the only
rooftop pool in Providence.

13:11.869 --> 13:14.203
No offense, but this
place is awesome.

13:14.237 --> 13:15.988
I-I-- Where was
I supposed to be offended

13:16.022 --> 13:17.022
within that remark?

13:17.074 --> 13:18.490
Can we, can we leave, Lois?

13:18.524 --> 13:20.024
Actually, we are leaving.

13:20.059 --> 13:22.360
We're hitting another
insane party across town.

13:22.395 --> 13:23.694
What, you mean now?

13:23.728 --> 13:25.763
Peter, you sound
like an old fart.

13:25.797 --> 13:28.097
I thought you liked
having a hot, young wife.

13:28.132 --> 13:30.999
Well, I did at first,
but the novelty's worn off.

13:31.033 --> 13:34.202
Same thing happened with
that blog I started on 9/11.

13:47.080 --> 13:49.230
Look, Peter,
you do what you want to do,

13:49.264 --> 13:50.698
but I'm going to that party.

13:50.733 --> 13:52.900
My life isn't over.
It's just beginning.

13:52.935 --> 13:55.403
So if you don't want
to run with the wild horses,

13:55.437 --> 13:58.088
then go back to the barn
and go to bed.

13:58.122 --> 14:00.589
But, Lois...

14:03.093 --> 14:05.560
Stupid place still doesn't
have my dry cleaning.

14:05.594 --> 14:07.996
That's not a dry cleaners.
It's a dance club.

14:08.030 --> 14:09.163
It is?

14:09.197 --> 14:11.432
Well, that explains a lot.

14:12.467 --> 14:13.499
(phone ringing)

14:13.534 --> 14:15.535
Oh, this is my jam!

14:24.001 --> 14:25.834
Jeez, Peter, you
look terrible.

14:25.835 --> 14:27.436
I know.
Lois has been wearing me out.

14:27.470 --> 14:28.871
I just can't keep up with her.

14:28.905 --> 14:30.672
I don't know what
she's trying to prove, Brian,

14:30.706 --> 14:31.874
but I can't take it anymore.

14:31.908 --> 14:33.042
Peter, can't you see?

14:33.076 --> 14:34.475
<i>She's doing this
because of you.</i>

14:34.510 --> 14:36.477
For God's sake, you
called her a plow horse.

14:36.512 --> 14:38.845
It's no wonder she's trying to
prove she's young and vibrant.

14:38.880 --> 14:40.414
(over TV):
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker.

14:40.448 --> 14:42.081
The city of Quahog
has been stricken

14:42.115 --> 14:43.950
with a case of Bieber Fever
tonight,

14:43.984 --> 14:46.885
as teen idol and fake black guy
Justin Bieber

14:46.919 --> 14:49.421
is in town for a sold-out show
at the Quahog Civic Center.

14:49.455 --> 14:50.821
We now go live

14:50.855 --> 14:53.023
to Asian correspondent
Tricia Takanawa with more.

14:53.058 --> 14:54.724
(girls screaming)
Tom, I'm standing here

14:54.758 --> 14:56.409
at the Quahog Civic Center,

14:56.460 --> 15:00.095
awash in a pool
of prepubescent sexual moisture.

15:00.129 --> 15:03.147
Woo-hoo!
We love you, Justin!

15:03.181 --> 15:04.465
Look!
That's Mom!

15:04.499 --> 15:06.200
Oh, my God!
What the hell?

15:06.235 --> 15:07.834
She's at
a Justin Bieber concert?

15:07.868 --> 15:10.036
Ugh, Justin Bieber's
so yesterday.

15:10.071 --> 15:12.305
I'm all about
Quentin Vashay now.

15:12.340 --> 15:13.707
Who's Quentin Vashay?

15:13.741 --> 15:15.075
Exactly.

15:15.109 --> 15:16.075
What's going on?

15:16.109 --> 15:18.277
Do we have to get
a new mom now?

15:18.311 --> 15:19.278
No, Chris.

15:19.312 --> 15:21.095
I'm gonna go get
our old mom back.

15:21.130 --> 15:23.131
If I'm the one
who made her feel this way,

15:23.165 --> 15:24.998
then I'm the one
who's got to fix it.

15:25.033 --> 15:26.617
Brian, keys!

15:26.651 --> 15:28.050
Chris, beer!

15:28.085 --> 15:30.052
Meg, ugly!

15:32.405 --> 15:33.939
Mm-hmm. Yes.

15:33.973 --> 15:35.473
Yes, I see.

15:35.508 --> 15:36.974
Rupert, the man
from the newspaper

15:36.976 --> 15:39.510
would like a quote from you
about my dancing abilities.

15:39.544 --> 15:40.843
Rupert?

15:40.878 --> 15:43.296
Where'd you go?

15:43.330 --> 15:45.330
Magnolia Cupcakes?

15:46.983 --> 15:47.966
(screams)

15:48.001 --> 15:49.367
Rupert! Oh, my God!

15:49.401 --> 15:50.835
Oh, my God, no!

15:50.869 --> 15:53.404
If he did this to you,
I swear I'll kill him!

15:53.438 --> 15:56.407
And what's that box from
Bloomingdale's doing here?

15:58.726 --> 16:02.294
I, uh, I-I don't know
who this is.

16:02.329 --> 16:05.331
(crowd cheering)

16:10.168 --> 16:12.752
(women screaming)

16:12.770 --> 16:15.087
Oh, my God, he is so adorable.

16:15.105 --> 16:17.256
I could just bite him
and eat him up.

16:17.274 --> 16:18.807
I know, he's perfect.

16:18.858 --> 16:20.475
He's like a boy
and a girl.

16:20.526 --> 16:21.893
I know!

16:21.927 --> 16:24.478
(women screaming)

16:29.483 --> 16:30.816
Sorry, you're not
allowed in here.

16:30.850 --> 16:32.250
Oh, yeah?

16:33.270 --> 16:34.836
I'm not into that.

16:34.871 --> 16:35.904
Oh.

16:35.938 --> 16:37.706
Well, what
are you into?

16:37.740 --> 16:39.106
Pinkberry.

16:39.124 --> 16:40.324
I love my job.

16:40.359 --> 16:42.877
Yum, yum, yum, yum,
yum, yum, yum, yum.

16:45.046 --> 16:46.946
Hey, there, cutie.

16:46.981 --> 16:48.814
Oh, hey. How's it going?

16:48.848 --> 16:50.766
Um, are you a friend
of my mom's?

16:50.800 --> 16:52.033
(chuckles)

16:52.067 --> 16:55.686
Yeah. I'm your mom's friend,
Mrs. Robinson.

16:55.720 --> 16:57.254
I don't... I don't get that.

16:57.288 --> 16:58.622
Is that a reference
to something?

16:58.656 --> 16:59.889
Uh, okay.

16:59.923 --> 17:02.525
Uh, I'm, uh-- oh,
I'm Stifler's mom.

17:02.559 --> 17:04.025
Still no idea.

17:04.060 --> 17:05.960
Okay, just get
your pants off, hon.

17:05.995 --> 17:07.862
Stop right there!
Get away from her!

17:07.897 --> 17:08.962
Peter?!
Who are you?

17:08.997 --> 17:10.197
How'd you get in here?

17:10.231 --> 17:13.349
Step away from my wife,
you acorn-penised beauty!

17:13.384 --> 17:15.185
Look, I swear.
Nothing happened.

17:15.220 --> 17:16.387
Just relax, old man.

17:16.421 --> 17:17.904
Old man?!

17:17.938 --> 17:20.989
What, you think you're not gonna
get old, you little bastard?!

17:21.024 --> 17:23.008
And, Lois, I've had
enough of you, too!

17:23.042 --> 17:25.242
Now, you come home
and start acting your age!

17:25.277 --> 17:27.211
No, Peter. I don't
want to act my age,

17:27.245 --> 17:28.746
and you don't
want that either.

17:28.780 --> 17:31.448
Otherwise, you wouldn't have
called me an old plow horse.

17:31.482 --> 17:33.033
Look, I didn't mean
to say that.

17:33.067 --> 17:34.283
I-I was a jerk.

17:34.317 --> 17:36.051
But isn't this
what you want?

17:36.086 --> 17:38.436
Don't you want me to
stay young and exciting?

17:38.470 --> 17:39.704
Well, I thought I did.

17:39.755 --> 17:41.506
I mean, every guy
who's been married a while

17:41.540 --> 17:42.956
thinks he wants
a hot, young chick,

17:42.990 --> 17:44.925
but after you spend an hour
with one of them,

17:44.959 --> 17:46.292
you want to blow
your brains out.

17:46.326 --> 17:49.528
But, Peter, I was just
doing this to make you happy.

17:49.563 --> 17:51.262
You do make me happy, Lois.

17:51.297 --> 17:53.665
You're the best thing
that's ever happened to me.

17:53.699 --> 17:54.999
That's sweet.

17:55.034 --> 17:57.736
But you got to admit,
I'm not what I used to be.

17:57.770 --> 17:58.869
Well, neither am I.

17:58.903 --> 18:00.554
(roars)

18:00.588 --> 18:02.239
I used to be
a lion tamer.

18:02.273 --> 18:04.374
Look, Lois,
I'll always treasure

18:04.408 --> 18:06.975
the wild, little hottie
I met when I was young.

18:07.009 --> 18:09.177
But I don't want to be
with a kid anymore.

18:09.195 --> 18:12.813
I want a smart, sexy, beautiful,
middle-aged companion.

18:12.847 --> 18:14.681
I want the real Lois.

18:14.699 --> 18:15.882
My Lois.

18:15.916 --> 18:17.617
Oh, Peter.

18:20.854 --> 18:24.005
Mr. Bieber, they're
calling for an encore!

18:25.507 --> 18:27.841
Oh, my God, those kids
are expecting a show.

18:27.875 --> 18:29.226
I'll handle this.

18:29.260 --> 18:31.244
(crowd cheering)

18:33.080 --> 18:36.832
Ladies and gentlemen,
Mr. Conway Bieber.

18:36.866 --> 18:41.369
♪ People see us everywhere

18:41.387 --> 18:45.472
♪ They think you really care

18:45.507 --> 18:49.926
♪ But myself I can't deceive

18:49.977 --> 18:55.981
♪ I know it's only
make-believe... ♪

19:11.276 --> 19:14.044
(air hissing)

19:14.078 --> 19:17.914
STEWIE: Well, well,
look who has surfaced.

19:21.502 --> 19:23.652
You're getting colder.

19:30.959 --> 19:32.142
(yells)

19:33.744 --> 19:35.077
(hisses)

19:37.848 --> 19:39.030
(hisses)

19:39.065 --> 19:40.999
Hey, get out here
and fight me!

19:47.188 --> 19:49.255
(screams)

19:52.275 --> 19:54.443
(coughs)

19:55.562 --> 19:56.595
Damn it!

20:03.035 --> 20:07.003
Now batting:
Stewie Griffin!

20:07.038 --> 20:08.771
(beeping steadily)

20:08.805 --> 20:10.206
Oh, crap.

20:19.781 --> 20:22.682
Ugh, you look like
a nude Larry David.

20:22.716 --> 20:24.883
No, no, no!

20:24.917 --> 20:26.234
(video game sound effects)

20:26.269 --> 20:27.702
Oh, my God, Super Mario?

20:27.737 --> 20:29.170
What are you doing here?

20:29.204 --> 20:30.905
(Italian accent):
I jump on a turtle, Stewie.

20:30.939 --> 20:34.340
It's not an exciting life,
but it's my life.

20:37.344 --> 20:39.512
It sure is good to
have you back, Mom.

20:39.547 --> 20:41.114
Yeah, we missed you.

20:41.148 --> 20:43.215
Well, thanks for putting up
with me, you guys.

20:43.249 --> 20:45.850
Sorry I got so flipped out
about my age.

20:45.884 --> 20:47.418
Aw, don't worry
about it, Lois.

20:47.452 --> 20:48.920
But from now on,
remember:

20:48.954 --> 20:51.321
I love you just
the way you are.

20:51.355 --> 20:53.657
And besides, there's nothing
wrong with being 35.

20:53.691 --> 20:56.025
Peter, I'm 43.

20:56.059 --> 20:57.860
Get out of this house.

20:57.861 --> 21:58.861
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru